// RT_MANIFEST must be the NUMERIC type id 24. A bare `.rc` compiled by
// rc.exe does not include winres.h, so the identifier `RT_MANIFEST` would be
// emitted as a NAMED resource type (the string "RT_MANIFEST") instead of the
// numeric 24 the Windows loader looks up for the application manifest. With a
// named type, the loader cannot find the manifest, treats the exe as
// manifest-less, and UAC's installer-detection heuristics raise a consent
// prompt on every run (seen empirically on the updater-compat harness).
1 24 "app.manifest"
